Read the client IP from the SAPI, so PHP-FPM incidents carry it (GH #2262)

get_ipaddr() reads REMOTE_ADDR with getenv(). Under PHP-FPM the request's
REMOTE_ADDR is a FastCGI parameter, not part of the process environment,
so every web request read as 0.0.0.0: in log lines, and for .cidr() rule
matching. Ask the SAPI first; the old lookups stay as the fallback (CLI,
and FPM before it starts serving).

Applied at build time by ../apply-patches.sh (all patches or none).
Upstream: https://github.com/jvoisin/snuffleupagus

--- a/src/sp_utils.c
+++ b/src/sp_utils.c
@@ -10,6 +10,25 @@
 
 static char const* const default_ipaddr = "0.0.0.0";
 const char* get_ipaddr() {
+  // Jabali (GH #2262): under PHP-FPM, REMOTE_ADDR is a FastCGI parameter,
+  // not part of the process environment, so the getenv() below never finds
+  // it and every web request read as 0.0.0.0. Ask the SAPI first, for
+  // REMOTE_ADDR only: the web server sets it, while X-Forwarded-For is
+  // whatever the client sent. sapi_getenv() returns a copy to free.
+  ZEND_TLS char sapi_ip[64];
+  char* const sapi_val = sapi_getenv("REMOTE_ADDR", sizeof("REMOTE_ADDR") - 1);
+  if (sapi_val) {
+    const size_t len = strlen(sapi_val);
+    const bool fits = len > 0 && len < sizeof(sapi_ip);
+    if (fits) {
+      memcpy(sapi_ip, sapi_val, len + 1);
+    }
+    efree(sapi_val);
+    if (fits) {
+      return sapi_ip;
+    }
+  }
+
   const char* client_ip = getenv("REMOTE_ADDR");
   if (client_ip) {
     return client_ip;
